1
00:00:02,002 --> 00:00:03,069
<i>Michiko!</i>

2
00:00:09,743 --> 00:00:12,112
I slept so well!

3
00:00:14,647 --> 00:00:16,716
Ben Casey! Gannon!

4
00:00:16,783 --> 00:00:18,485
You get along so well.

5
00:00:20,253 --> 00:00:21,421
Morning.

6
00:00:23,323 --> 00:00:24,491
What's wrong?

7
00:00:24,557 --> 00:00:26,359
Don't act like that.

8
00:00:26,426 --> 00:00:28,161
- What?
- What's your problem?

9
00:00:28,228 --> 00:00:29,229
What do you mean?

10
00:00:30,163 --> 00:00:31,264
Look at this!

11
00:00:31,331 --> 00:00:32,632
What?

12
00:00:32,699 --> 00:00:33,833
Hey!

13
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:36,169
I've seen this scary woman before.

14
00:00:36,236 --> 00:00:37,604
Who is she again?

15
00:00:37,670 --> 00:00:40,373
She's the Totei University PR Chief.

16
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:42,842
Oh, that's right!
So what did this lady do?

17
00:00:42,909 --> 00:00:45,145
- That's not what I mean.
- What?

18
00:00:45,211 --> 00:00:46,646
This!

19
00:00:46,713 --> 00:00:48,515
Where? My vision has been--

20
00:00:48,581 --> 00:00:50,150
That's you, right?

21
00:00:50,216 --> 00:00:51,618
I can't see.

22
00:00:54,487 --> 00:00:55,955
- Uh-oh.
- You…

23
00:00:56,022 --> 00:00:59,325
You said they had sold all the <i>takoyaki!</i>

24
00:00:59,392 --> 00:01:02,762
But here you are eating them all yourself!

25
00:01:02,829 --> 00:01:05,131
It was the last tray!

26
00:01:05,198 --> 00:01:07,734
I was going to bring
half of them back to you.

27
00:01:07,801 --> 00:01:10,103
- But they would get cold!
- Yes, sure. Cut the excuses!

28
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:12,105
I'm not making excuses!

29
00:01:12,172 --> 00:01:14,207
- I had just operated!
- You gluttonous woman!

30
00:01:14,274 --> 00:01:17,110
- I can't believe those excuses!
- I was so hungry.

31
00:01:17,177 --> 00:01:18,978
- But I'm always…
- Fine! I don't care!

32
00:01:19,045 --> 00:01:21,848
- I'm always operating for your sake!
- You're so selfish!

33
00:01:21,915 --> 00:01:23,516
- Fine! I don't care!
- That hurts!

34
00:01:23,583 --> 00:01:26,019
Hey! That hurts!

35
00:01:26,086 --> 00:01:28,121
I'm sorry…

36
00:01:28,621 --> 00:01:31,157
So what's for breakfast?

37
00:01:31,691 --> 00:01:35,028
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a maverick woman doctor.</i>

38
00:01:35,095 --> 00:01:36,396
What's for breakfast?

39
00:01:37,664 --> 00:01:39,599
<i>2021.</i>

40
00:01:39,666 --> 00:01:43,269
<i>The ravages</i>
<i>of a once-in-a-century pandemic</i>

41
00:01:43,336 --> 00:01:45,972
<i>have devastated</i>
<i>the world's medical systems.</i>

42
00:01:47,006 --> 00:01:48,541
<i>With the might of a cornered animal,</i>

43
00:01:48,608 --> 00:01:50,977
<i>Japan's medical universities</i>

44
00:01:51,044 --> 00:01:54,114
<i>have somehow weathered the storm.</i>

45
00:01:54,747 --> 00:01:56,049
DIRECTOR OF INTERNAL MEDICINE'S OFFICE

46
00:01:56,116 --> 00:01:57,317
Vice Minister Kanbe,

47
00:01:57,383 --> 00:02:01,488
I am terribly sorry for the trouble
this has caused you.

48
00:02:01,554 --> 00:02:03,389
We will deal with the press.

49
00:02:04,390 --> 00:02:08,394
Yes. I am very much aware of that.

50
00:02:09,329 --> 00:02:10,864
Yes. Thank you.

51
00:02:10,930 --> 00:02:12,198
Goodbye.

52
00:02:14,767 --> 00:02:15,969
I am very sorry.

53
00:02:22,509 --> 00:02:25,011
Suspicion of entertaining a bureaucrat

54
00:02:25,078 --> 00:02:28,781
is the kind of scandal that offends
the general public the most!

55
00:02:29,549 --> 00:02:31,818
You were far too careless.

56
00:02:31,885 --> 00:02:33,586
That's not like you.

57
00:02:37,090 --> 00:02:40,727
Were you able to get
Vice Minister Kanbe to promise us…

58
00:02:42,128 --> 00:02:43,363
a scientific research grant?

59
00:02:45,565 --> 00:02:46,666
No.

60
00:02:47,367 --> 00:02:48,801
- We didn't…
- You fool!

61
00:02:49,569 --> 00:02:55,575
To bring about the new internal medicine
treatment method, chemical surgery,

62
00:02:56,576 --> 00:02:59,245
an increase in grant money is necessary!

63
00:02:59,879 --> 00:03:01,314
Arranging a dinner meeting

64
00:03:01,381 --> 00:03:04,184
with the vice minister
at a time like this was…

65
00:03:05,118 --> 00:03:07,353
for that purpose, wasn't it?

66
00:03:09,489 --> 00:03:10,757
Yes, it was.

67
00:03:14,194 --> 00:03:15,595
You know,

68
00:03:16,196 --> 00:03:18,131
you can be easily replaced.

69
00:03:20,466 --> 00:03:21,901
I'll make up for this!

70
00:03:22,535 --> 00:03:25,838
Straighten things out nicely
so that Totei University…

71
00:03:26,406 --> 00:03:29,709
and the Ministry of Health are not harmed.

72
00:03:34,047 --> 00:03:35,248
Make sure that…

73
00:03:35,848 --> 00:03:39,419
this isn't your last task here.

74
00:03:40,553 --> 00:03:41,654
Understand?

75
00:03:44,457 --> 00:03:45,892
Yes, sir.

76
00:03:57,870 --> 00:03:59,072
There she is!

77
00:03:59,138 --> 00:04:00,273
Ms. Mikuni!

78
00:04:03,376 --> 00:04:05,612
This is a hospital!

79
00:04:05,678 --> 00:04:07,413
Please be quiet!

80
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:09,515
Was your dinner with Vice Minister Kanbe

81
00:04:09,582 --> 00:04:11,517
to pressure him for grant money?

82
00:04:11,584 --> 00:04:13,253
Did Acting Director Hachisuka order this?

83
00:04:13,319 --> 00:04:14,554
No!

84
00:04:14,621 --> 00:04:16,122
It was not a business dinner.

85
00:04:16,689 --> 00:04:20,493
<i>Meanwhile, this freelance maverick doctor…</i>

86
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:24,831
<i>who was never attached</i>
<i>to any hospital returned.</i>

87
00:04:25,465 --> 00:04:28,801
- Didn't you realize that was illegal?
- I told you, it was not…

88
00:04:33,239 --> 00:04:34,941
- What's wrong?
- What's the matter?

89
00:04:35,008 --> 00:04:36,109
Out of the way!

90
00:04:37,176 --> 00:04:38,478
Are you okay?

91
00:04:39,178 --> 00:04:40,346
Give me that.

92
00:04:45,551 --> 00:04:47,854
- Possible ACS. Stretcher!
- Right!

93
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:49,122
- Stat!
- Right!

94
00:04:49,188 --> 00:04:52,625
Can you believe this?
Using the hospital to her benefit.

95
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:55,895
<i>She hates groups,</i>

96
00:04:55,962 --> 00:04:59,165
<i>she hates authorities,</i>

97
00:04:59,232 --> 00:05:01,100
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

98
00:05:01,167 --> 00:05:04,470
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill</i>

99
00:05:04,537 --> 00:05:05,805
<i> to work her way up.</i>

100
00:05:13,946 --> 00:05:17,016
We'll take care of this from here.

101
00:05:17,083 --> 00:05:18,351
Why?

102
00:05:18,418 --> 00:05:21,120
The patient is this hospital's PR Chief

103
00:05:21,187 --> 00:05:23,323
and the acting director's right hand.

104
00:05:23,389 --> 00:05:25,625
Internal medicine will handle
the treatment.

105
00:05:31,931 --> 00:05:33,533
- Take her to Emergency Room.
- Right.

106
00:05:45,044 --> 00:05:46,045
CLINICAL EXAMINATION

107
00:05:46,112 --> 00:05:47,180
Hey!

108
00:05:47,847 --> 00:05:50,717
You're in cahoots
with that woman, aren't you?

109
00:05:50,783 --> 00:05:51,684
What?

110
00:05:55,355 --> 00:05:56,656
- Got it.
- Okay.

111
00:05:56,723 --> 00:05:58,291
- Get a blood sample.
- Right.

112
00:05:58,358 --> 00:06:00,760
You eluded the press nicely.

113
00:06:01,494 --> 00:06:02,995
That was the right thing to do.

114
00:06:09,068 --> 00:06:11,137
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

115
00:06:11,704 --> 00:06:15,141
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

116
00:06:33,259 --> 00:06:37,897
SURGERY BRANCH

117
00:06:44,604 --> 00:06:46,706
She collapsed on purpose?

118
00:06:46,773 --> 00:06:47,874
I'm certain of it.

119
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:51,611
She's using the hospital as cover
to deal with the situation?

120
00:06:51,677 --> 00:06:53,346
She's pretending to be sick!

121
00:06:54,714 --> 00:06:59,819
But wasn't it Michiko Daimon
who diagnosed her at first?

122
00:07:00,386 --> 00:07:02,422
- Possible ACS. Stretcher!
- Right!

123
00:07:02,488 --> 00:07:03,723
- Stat!
- Right!

124
00:07:04,857 --> 00:07:07,059
That is the issue.

125
00:07:10,196 --> 00:07:12,131
Look at this.

126
00:07:12,198 --> 00:07:13,833
What? This woman?

127
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:15,435
Oh, that's Dr. Daimon.

128
00:07:15,501 --> 00:07:18,604
This crude way of eating
means it can only be Dr. Daimon!

129
00:07:18,671 --> 00:07:21,474
But why is Dr. Daimon in this photo?

130
00:07:21,541 --> 00:07:23,409
This same Dr. Daimon

131
00:07:23,910 --> 00:07:27,747
saved PR Chief Mikuni
when she collapsed in the hospital lobby.

132
00:07:28,548 --> 00:07:30,583
I highly doubt it's a coincidence.

133
00:07:31,184 --> 00:07:34,387
You mean Michiko Daimon also had dinner

134
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:36,689
at this illegal entertainment
of a bureaucrat?

135
00:07:36,756 --> 00:07:38,891
I believe it's highly likely.

136
00:07:38,958 --> 00:07:41,527
She can be easily enticed with food.

137
00:07:41,594 --> 00:07:45,631
And PR Chief Mikuni
conspired with Dr. Daimon

138
00:07:45,698 --> 00:07:47,366
to take this drastic measure.

139
00:07:47,867 --> 00:07:52,004
Director Hachisuka is cold,
and he will stop at nothing.

140
00:07:52,071 --> 00:07:54,507
If the situation can't be dealt with,

141
00:07:55,708 --> 00:08:00,480
even PR Chief Mikuni could be cut off
like a lizard's tail.

142
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:03,049
How frightening.

143
00:08:03,115 --> 00:08:04,617
Cut off like a lizard's tail.

144
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:06,519
I'm so envious.

145
00:08:07,119 --> 00:08:11,824
Director of Internal Medicine Hachisuka
is lucky to have a tail

146
00:08:11,891 --> 00:08:13,526
he can cut off when he likes.

147
00:08:14,460 --> 00:08:15,328
What?

148
00:08:15,394 --> 00:08:21,501
I was just wondering
if I had a tail like that too.

149
00:08:21,567 --> 00:08:25,171
Branch Director Hiruma,
are you saying you want us

150
00:08:25,238 --> 00:08:27,406
to have illegal dinners with bureaucrats?

151
00:08:27,473 --> 00:08:29,775
No, I'm not saying that.

152
00:08:29,842 --> 00:08:31,711
But scientific research grants,

153
00:08:32,712 --> 00:08:33,713
that's something…

154
00:08:35,248 --> 00:08:38,885
I would like
for the Surgery Department too.

155
00:08:43,356 --> 00:08:45,558
We will now begin the combined conference.

156
00:08:46,359 --> 00:08:48,561
Go ahead, Vice Director Kuwagata.

157
00:08:51,364 --> 00:08:56,502
The patient is this hospital's
PR Chief Choko Mikuni, age 55.

158
00:08:56,569 --> 00:08:59,372
Today, she complained of chest pain
in the lobby.

159
00:08:59,438 --> 00:09:01,207
The symptoms soon subsided,

160
00:09:01,274 --> 00:09:03,175
but the pain reappeared.

161
00:09:03,242 --> 00:09:06,212
So we ran tests to check for ischemia.

162
00:09:10,750 --> 00:09:13,486
I guess PR Chief Mikuni is actually sick.

163
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:17,423
Damn. I guess it wasn't faked
beforehand then.

164
00:09:22,295 --> 00:09:23,896
It's a Takotsubo.

165
00:09:23,963 --> 00:09:25,431
"Takotsubo?"

166
00:09:25,498 --> 00:09:26,899
"Takotsubo?"

167
00:09:26,966 --> 00:09:28,834
Dr. Daimon, I will explain.

168
00:09:29,702 --> 00:09:30,770
Fine.

169
00:09:31,804 --> 00:09:33,306
She has been diagnosed with…

170
00:09:34,006 --> 00:09:35,441
Takotsubo cardiomyopathy.

171
00:09:36,208 --> 00:09:38,511
It does look like an octopus jar trap.

172
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:42,548
It is also known as stress cardiomyopathy

173
00:09:42,615 --> 00:09:44,650
caused by either systolic dysfunction

174
00:09:44,717 --> 00:09:46,385
or outflow tract stenosis.

175
00:09:46,452 --> 00:09:48,054
We must determine which.

176
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:49,822
From observing the video,

177
00:09:50,389 --> 00:09:53,359
I believe the patient
has systolic dysfunction.

178
00:09:53,426 --> 00:09:55,361
Even from a surgery perspective,

179
00:09:55,428 --> 00:09:59,599
a short-acting beta-blocker IV

180
00:09:59,665 --> 00:10:01,567
would be the best treatment.

181
00:10:01,634 --> 00:10:03,269
In other words,

182
00:10:03,336 --> 00:10:06,305
this patient should be treated
with internal medicine methods?

183
00:10:06,872 --> 00:10:07,840
Yes.

184
00:10:08,841 --> 00:10:10,710
Dr. Korogi is on Internal Medicine's side.

185
00:10:10,776 --> 00:10:13,145
He has been their tool from the start.

186
00:10:13,212 --> 00:10:16,415
Is pheochromocytoma
or cerebrovascular disease possible?

187
00:10:17,683 --> 00:10:20,586
We ran tests,
but we didn't find evidence of those.

188
00:10:21,153 --> 00:10:24,256
Then it must be excitability
of the sympathetic nerves.

189
00:10:25,291 --> 00:10:26,826
Let's take this patient.

190
00:10:27,493 --> 00:10:28,427
What?

191
00:10:28,494 --> 00:10:30,396
Any questions or opinions?

192
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:32,865
If the Surgery Department
cures PR Chief Mikuni,

193
00:10:32,932 --> 00:10:35,868
we could draw research grants our way.

194
00:10:36,469 --> 00:10:37,436
I see.

195
00:10:38,804 --> 00:10:39,872
Go, Kaji!

196
00:10:39,939 --> 00:10:41,207
Objection!

197
00:10:43,209 --> 00:10:45,277
Careless administration of a beta-blocker

198
00:10:45,344 --> 00:10:48,614
could cause left ventricle
outflow tract stenosis.

199
00:10:48,681 --> 00:10:51,851
That means Internal Medicine
shouldn't be handling this?

200
00:10:51,917 --> 00:10:52,818
Right.

201
00:10:52,885 --> 00:10:53,719
Also,

202
00:10:53,786 --> 00:10:55,755
though it is not a comorbidity,

203
00:10:55,821 --> 00:10:56,856
the patient…

204
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:06,132
The patient has moderate stenosis
in the left coronary artery branch.

205
00:11:06,866 --> 00:11:09,602
The Surgery Department believes
it is best to…

206
00:11:10,102 --> 00:11:14,740
conduct a coronary bypass surgery
to prevent further problems.

207
00:11:14,807 --> 00:11:16,642
Well said! Excellent proposal!

208
00:11:16,709 --> 00:11:18,678
Right? Everyone applaud!

209
00:11:20,479 --> 00:11:23,683
The director and vice director
are working like a tag team.

210
00:11:24,283 --> 00:11:25,818
What an obvious farce.

211
00:11:27,553 --> 00:11:29,422
Is that surgery even necessary?

212
00:11:30,256 --> 00:11:32,458
That stenosis isn't bad enough
to operate on.

213
00:11:33,225 --> 00:11:35,061
You call yourself a surgeon?

214
00:11:35,127 --> 00:11:38,164
The Surgery Department
just wants to operate.

215
00:11:38,230 --> 00:11:41,934
Not everything can be cured
with just medicine!

216
00:11:42,001 --> 00:11:43,803
Think about the risks of side effects!

217
00:11:46,405 --> 00:11:47,907
I'm hungry.

218
00:11:49,308 --> 00:11:51,977
Dr. Daimon!

219
00:11:52,044 --> 00:11:54,246
Dr. Daimon!

220
00:11:54,313 --> 00:11:55,314
What would you do?

221
00:11:55,381 --> 00:11:56,582
About what?

222
00:11:56,649 --> 00:11:58,417
What treatment would you do?

223
00:11:58,484 --> 00:12:00,019
You want to operate, right?

224
00:12:01,520 --> 00:12:02,822
No, I won't.

225
00:12:03,389 --> 00:12:04,657
Hey, hold on!

226
00:12:04,724 --> 00:12:06,959
Yes, you will. Dr. Daimon!

227
00:12:07,026 --> 00:12:08,427
I knew it.

228
00:12:08,494 --> 00:12:10,563
She's in cahoots with Internal Medicine.

229
00:12:10,629 --> 00:12:14,266
This is not just an issue

230
00:12:14,333 --> 00:12:17,269
of our hospital's great PR chief
becoming ill.

231
00:12:17,336 --> 00:12:19,672
This is a major case
that affects confidence

232
00:12:19,739 --> 00:12:21,540
in Totei University Hospital.

233
00:12:22,274 --> 00:12:24,243
Acting Hospital Director Hachisuka

234
00:12:24,310 --> 00:12:28,614
has ordered that Internal Medicine
be in charge of the treatment.

235
00:12:30,449 --> 00:12:31,517
Understand?

236
00:12:34,887 --> 00:12:36,155
There it is again.

237
00:12:36,222 --> 00:12:38,224
The "yes, sir" pose
that doesn't spray droplets.

238
00:12:39,859 --> 00:12:41,127
Like this.

239
00:12:41,193 --> 00:12:44,263
What the heck are you doing?

240
00:12:44,330 --> 00:12:45,865
We were just…

241
00:12:48,901 --> 00:12:51,303
Director of Internal Medicine Hachisuka.

242
00:12:52,671 --> 00:12:53,873
I see…

243
00:12:55,074 --> 00:13:00,146
you've learned to make deals
in a very grown-up way.

244
00:13:00,946 --> 00:13:02,281
But…

245
00:13:05,050 --> 00:13:06,418
this is not good.

246
00:13:06,485 --> 00:13:09,722
I bet this sent a shock
through the Ministry of Health.

247
00:13:09,789 --> 00:13:11,290
What a nuisance.

248
00:13:12,224 --> 00:13:14,426
That was just our usual sharing
of information.

249
00:13:14,994 --> 00:13:16,762
There is absolutely nothing…

250
00:13:17,563 --> 00:13:19,031
for you to worry about.

251
00:13:19,532 --> 00:13:20,833
Do you really think so?

252
00:13:23,102 --> 00:13:24,837
What do you mean?

253
00:13:24,904 --> 00:13:27,173
For people like you…

254
00:13:27,239 --> 00:13:31,844
who always demand 100% perfection…

255
00:13:33,112 --> 00:13:34,547
How can I put this?

256
00:13:35,848 --> 00:13:40,452
You lack flexibility in your soul.

257
00:13:42,521 --> 00:13:45,491
You're always worried about the results…

258
00:13:46,125 --> 00:13:48,627
and are burdened
with huge amounts of stress.

259
00:13:50,629 --> 00:13:52,832
I don't know what you're talking about.

260
00:13:52,898 --> 00:13:55,100
I'm worried about you.

261
00:13:56,402 --> 00:13:57,570
Though,

262
00:13:57,636 --> 00:14:00,105
in the medical world,

263
00:14:01,273 --> 00:14:04,510
your type is something
we cannot do without.

264
00:14:05,644 --> 00:14:07,646
And of course,

265
00:14:07,713 --> 00:14:10,416
here at Totei University Hospital as well.

266
00:14:13,719 --> 00:14:15,454
Thank you.

267
00:14:17,256 --> 00:14:19,692
I have another meeting.

268
00:14:19,758 --> 00:14:20,860
I see.

269
00:14:22,094 --> 00:14:23,762
Hey…

270
00:14:23,829 --> 00:14:28,801
Because it has been a while
since I came all the way over,

271
00:14:28,868 --> 00:14:30,703
can I stay here a little longer?

272
00:14:31,403 --> 00:14:32,738
Feel free.

273
00:14:33,305 --> 00:14:34,206
Thank you.

274
00:14:45,484 --> 00:14:49,288
This room is wasted on that flunky.

275
00:14:53,459 --> 00:14:56,095
You have Takotsubo cardiomyopathy.

276
00:14:56,161 --> 00:14:58,297
Caused by excitability
of the sympathetic nerves.

277
00:14:58,364 --> 00:14:59,798
In other words, stress.

278
00:15:00,366 --> 00:15:01,200
Stress?

279
00:15:01,767 --> 00:15:04,603
The perfect illness to help you escape.

280
00:15:05,638 --> 00:15:07,539
It's no surprise that you're stressed.

281
00:15:08,140 --> 00:15:10,142
Director of Internal Medicine Hachisuka

282
00:15:10,209 --> 00:15:12,678
always has you under a lot of stress.

283
00:15:12,745 --> 00:15:15,014
I would be too afraid to do…

284
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:16,916
that illegal entertainment.

285
00:15:17,416 --> 00:15:19,285
It's just part of the job.

286
00:15:20,085 --> 00:15:20,920
Well,

287
00:15:20,986 --> 00:15:22,021
you may as well

288
00:15:22,087 --> 00:15:25,391
take it easy
until the commotion dies down.

289
00:15:25,457 --> 00:15:27,326
Don't underestimate it.

290
00:15:30,162 --> 00:15:32,798
You should know
that Takotsubo cardiomyopathy

291
00:15:32,865 --> 00:15:34,900
can cause a cardiac rupture.

292
00:15:34,967 --> 00:15:35,968
In other words,

293
00:15:36,035 --> 00:15:38,437
it's a dangerous disease
you could die from.

294
00:15:39,138 --> 00:15:40,005
Die?

295
00:15:40,072 --> 00:15:42,074
What an exaggeration.

296
00:15:42,141 --> 00:15:44,543
We're administering a beta-blocker.

297
00:15:44,610 --> 00:15:47,079
Don't give the patient unnecessary stress.

298
00:15:47,146 --> 00:15:49,415
You're my biggest cause of stress.

299
00:15:49,949 --> 00:15:51,450
Why don't you get out?

300
00:15:51,517 --> 00:15:53,585
Let's see…

301
00:15:53,652 --> 00:15:56,488
Heart rate and blood pressure are fine.

302
00:15:57,489 --> 00:15:59,558
Even with me here,
you show no signs of stress.

303
00:16:00,759 --> 00:16:02,161
At any rate,

304
00:16:02,227 --> 00:16:03,595
make sure you rest.

305
00:16:11,503 --> 00:16:13,605
<i>I can't believe that PR Chief Mikuni</i>

306
00:16:13,672 --> 00:16:15,341
got Takotsubo from stress.

307
00:16:15,407 --> 00:16:18,110
- Can't judge a book by its cover.
- Yes.

308
00:16:18,177 --> 00:16:22,047
That's a tough job,
so she must have to put up with a lot.

309
00:16:22,114 --> 00:16:24,883
But she is the last person

310
00:16:24,950 --> 00:16:27,987
I would expect to get stressed
because of work.

311
00:16:28,053 --> 00:16:29,388
How come?

312
00:16:30,255 --> 00:16:33,092
She graduated from
the Totei University School of Economics

313
00:16:33,158 --> 00:16:34,460
at the top of her class.

314
00:16:34,526 --> 00:16:36,628
The instant she joined Toto Bank,

315
00:16:36,695 --> 00:16:39,798
she showed results
and distinguished herself.

316
00:16:39,865 --> 00:16:43,569
Then she was headhunted
for a variety of industries,

317
00:16:43,635 --> 00:16:47,573
<i>and built her career off successes</i>
<i>in business.</i>

318
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:50,075
<i>It's said that</i>

319
00:16:50,142 --> 00:16:54,313
<i>she's a woman who turns</i>
<i>work stress into energy.</i>

320
00:16:54,813 --> 00:16:56,515
Then what caused the Takotsubo?

321
00:16:56,582 --> 00:16:57,783
Oh, come on.

322
00:16:57,850 --> 00:17:00,552
Just living, there's always
some kind of stress.

323
00:17:00,619 --> 00:17:01,720
She's human, after all.

324
00:17:02,254 --> 00:17:04,823
- That's a nice Mitsuo Aida quote.
- Tell me!

325
00:17:04,890 --> 00:17:06,258
What stresses you, Akira?

326
00:17:06,325 --> 00:17:08,727
What stresses me? Well…

327
00:17:08,794 --> 00:17:10,863
What? You'll tell only me?

328
00:17:10,929 --> 00:17:12,331
- I knew it!
- What?

329
00:17:12,398 --> 00:17:13,665
Michiko!

330
00:17:13,732 --> 00:17:15,534
- Don't! You can see my tiles!
- How come?

331
00:17:15,601 --> 00:17:17,036
And you, Hiromi?

332
00:17:17,102 --> 00:17:17,936
Me?

333
00:17:18,003 --> 00:17:19,271
Oh, I know what it is!

334
00:17:20,439 --> 00:17:22,541
Michiko, go back!

335
00:17:22,608 --> 00:17:23,876
Don't you dare!

336
00:17:23,942 --> 00:17:25,477
- How come?
- Don't!

337
00:17:25,544 --> 00:17:28,113
- It gives me tons of stress!
- Oh, wow!

338
00:17:28,180 --> 00:17:30,115
- What's so surprising?
- Seriously?

339
00:17:30,182 --> 00:17:32,017
What gives you stress, Ms. Daimon?

340
00:17:32,084 --> 00:17:33,719
What gives me stress?

341
00:17:35,120 --> 00:17:37,656
What gives me stress is…

342
00:17:38,190 --> 00:17:40,092
- Nothing.
- Nothing?

343
00:17:40,159 --> 00:17:42,561
Then you're not human!

344
00:17:42,628 --> 00:17:44,730
Shut up!

345
00:17:44,797 --> 00:17:47,032
Michiko! That's <i>ron</i> for me!

346
00:17:47,099 --> 00:17:50,235
A triplet of dragons!

347
00:17:51,236 --> 00:17:55,340
Darn it! This is what gives me stress!

348
00:18:01,613 --> 00:18:03,082
YASHIRO KANBE, VICE MINISTER
OF HEALTH, LABOR, AND WELFARE

349
00:18:03,148 --> 00:18:05,784
Are you Vice Minister Kanbe
of the Ministry of Health?

350
00:18:05,851 --> 00:18:06,685
What?

351
00:18:07,186 --> 00:18:12,624
I am Dr. Ebina, Director of Surgery
at Totei University Hospital.

352
00:18:13,425 --> 00:18:17,563
I'm Dr. Kaji, Vice Director of Surgery
from the same hospital.

353
00:18:17,629 --> 00:18:21,366
We're terribly sorry about the trouble
our PR Chief Mikuni

354
00:18:21,433 --> 00:18:22,734
has caused you.

355
00:18:23,368 --> 00:18:26,605
We humbly apologize.

356
00:18:27,439 --> 00:18:29,108
What do you want?

357
00:18:29,675 --> 00:18:30,709
We're hoping…

358
00:18:31,276 --> 00:18:34,313
we can talk about
scientific research grant money.

359
00:18:35,981 --> 00:18:37,483
Don't you think

360
00:18:37,549 --> 00:18:40,586
talking about that in a place like this
is ill-advised?

361
00:18:40,652 --> 00:18:41,820
Goodbye.

362
00:18:41,887 --> 00:18:43,655
Vice Minister Kanbe!

363
00:18:43,722 --> 00:18:44,823
- Vice Minister!
- Wait!

364
00:18:44,890 --> 00:18:47,559
- Vice Minister!
- Quit shouting!

365
00:18:49,428 --> 00:18:51,363
Don't just favor Internal Medicine.

366
00:18:51,430 --> 00:18:54,433
Dine with Surgery a little too.
We know some good places.

367
00:18:54,500 --> 00:18:55,734
- Dr. Kaji!
- Right.

368
00:18:58,904 --> 00:19:01,573
Here is a little gift.

369
00:19:02,574 --> 00:19:04,910
I can't accept that!

370
00:19:05,477 --> 00:19:06,879
Please, take it.

371
00:19:06,945 --> 00:19:08,480
Not at a place like this!

372
00:19:08,547 --> 00:19:09,915
A Totei University towel.

373
00:19:10,649 --> 00:19:12,451
A Totei University pennant.

374
00:19:12,518 --> 00:19:14,486
Please have these.
They make for nice mementos.

375
00:19:14,553 --> 00:19:16,488
This is absolutely ridiculous!

376
00:19:20,092 --> 00:19:21,793
See?

377
00:19:21,860 --> 00:19:23,862
Didn't I tell you…

378
00:19:23,929 --> 00:19:25,864
But he does recognize us now.

379
00:19:27,533 --> 00:19:30,402
Now, we can be useful tails.

380
00:19:31,637 --> 00:19:32,738
Excellent.

381
00:19:37,042 --> 00:19:38,510
I got a complaint from…

382
00:19:39,745 --> 00:19:40,846
the Ministry of Health.

383
00:19:41,413 --> 00:19:42,247
What?

384
00:19:42,314 --> 00:19:43,348
A complaint?

385
00:19:43,415 --> 00:19:44,783
Apparently,

386
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:47,452
you invited Vice Minister Kanbe…

387
00:19:48,353 --> 00:19:50,255
out to dinner.

388
00:19:50,322 --> 00:19:51,356
Right?

389
00:19:52,024 --> 00:19:55,694
Why did you do such a thing?

390
00:19:55,761 --> 00:19:57,729
What? "Why?"

391
00:19:57,796 --> 00:20:00,799
I wanted to be a useful tail for you,
Branch Director Hiruma.

392
00:20:00,866 --> 00:20:02,067
Are you stupid?

393
00:20:02,634 --> 00:20:04,636
Who told you to be that kind of tail?

394
00:20:06,838 --> 00:20:07,906
What's the point…

395
00:20:09,074 --> 00:20:11,843
if my own tail causes me humiliation?

396
00:20:13,178 --> 00:20:14,246
Humiliation?

397
00:20:15,347 --> 00:20:17,549
I… I'm sorry!

398
00:20:17,616 --> 00:20:18,850
- I'll cut it off.
- What?

399
00:20:19,718 --> 00:20:22,588
I'll cut off this useless tail now.

400
00:20:23,622 --> 00:20:24,456
Yui!

401
00:20:25,023 --> 00:20:26,358
You have a knife?

402
00:20:27,292 --> 00:20:28,293
Yes.

403
00:20:28,827 --> 00:20:30,462
How about scissors?

404
00:20:30,529 --> 00:20:33,232
- That's fine.
- I told him not to do it.

405
00:20:33,899 --> 00:20:35,500
You're scared, aren't you?

406
00:20:35,567 --> 00:20:36,602
You can't go in.

407
00:20:36,668 --> 00:20:38,070
Can you, Dr. Kaji?

408
00:20:38,136 --> 00:20:39,805
My stomach hurts.

409
00:20:39,871 --> 00:20:41,206
I'll get some medicine.

410
00:20:41,273 --> 00:20:42,407
Excuse me.

411
00:20:42,474 --> 00:20:44,309
- Dr. Kaji is here.
- Hey!

412
00:20:46,645 --> 00:20:48,413
Hideki Kaji…

413
00:20:49,514 --> 00:20:50,882
I'm sorry!

414
00:20:52,618 --> 00:20:55,687
I am very sorry
for causing this situation.

415
00:20:55,754 --> 00:20:57,689
Is it okay for you to be out of bed?

416
00:20:58,190 --> 00:20:59,725
I will return to work soon

417
00:20:59,791 --> 00:21:01,727
and complete the mission
I've been assigned.

418
00:21:01,793 --> 00:21:02,995
Before that…

419
00:21:04,363 --> 00:21:08,333
I would like to consult you
about something.

420
00:21:09,101 --> 00:21:09,935
Yes?

421
00:21:10,636 --> 00:21:13,505
RESUME

422
00:21:14,339 --> 00:21:15,407
What are these?

423
00:21:15,474 --> 00:21:18,076
Candidates to become the new PR chief.

424
00:21:19,544 --> 00:21:22,547
So who would you choose?

425
00:21:24,383 --> 00:21:27,853
Are you saying
that you don't need me anymore?

426
00:21:27,919 --> 00:21:33,558
I believe that you need
to take some time off.

427
00:21:41,033 --> 00:21:44,503
It's still too soon for you to walk.
Lie down, would you?

428
00:21:44,569 --> 00:21:45,704
It's okay.

429
00:21:45,771 --> 00:21:47,205
I'm fine.

430
00:21:48,840 --> 00:21:51,643
There's no point in dying from your job.

431
00:21:51,710 --> 00:21:52,878
Don't be ridiculous.

432
00:21:53,445 --> 00:21:56,415
That doesn't give me
the least bit of stress.

433
00:22:05,791 --> 00:22:07,726
- How am I?
- Everything is fine.

434
00:22:08,760 --> 00:22:10,162
Didn't I tell you?

435
00:22:10,228 --> 00:22:12,064
My job isn't giving me stress.

436
00:22:13,332 --> 00:22:16,134
But it's still too soon
to go back to work.

437
00:22:16,201 --> 00:22:18,103
Media is there to worry about too.

438
00:22:18,837 --> 00:22:20,105
All right.

439
00:22:20,172 --> 00:22:22,174
So you're ordering me to get bed rest.

440
00:22:32,250 --> 00:22:33,418
Hello.

441
00:22:34,186 --> 00:22:35,220
Who are you?

442
00:22:36,755 --> 00:22:39,691
I am Vice Minister's Kanbe's wife!

443
00:22:40,726 --> 00:22:42,527
Vice Minister Kanbe's wife?

444
00:22:42,594 --> 00:22:46,898
For inviting my husband
to dinner the other evening,

445
00:22:47,599 --> 00:22:48,867
I thank you.

446
00:22:50,569 --> 00:22:51,603
What do you want?

447
00:22:52,971 --> 00:22:55,507
It's your fault
that things have gone crazy!

448
00:22:56,074 --> 00:22:58,610
Media people are practically
knocking down my door!

449
00:22:58,677 --> 00:23:00,545
I'm sorry for causing you trouble.

450
00:23:00,612 --> 00:23:01,713
However,

451
00:23:01,780 --> 00:23:03,615
it was not illegal entertainment.

452
00:23:03,682 --> 00:23:05,350
Not illegal?

453
00:23:05,851 --> 00:23:07,552
How can you say that?

454
00:23:08,387 --> 00:23:12,524
What you did was ethically illegal!

455
00:23:13,692 --> 00:23:16,762
You're nothing special…

456
00:23:17,996 --> 00:23:20,499
but you used your charm
to seduce my husband!

457
00:23:21,700 --> 00:23:22,768
An affair?

458
00:23:24,770 --> 00:23:27,038
You homewrecker!

459
00:23:27,105 --> 00:23:29,641
Stop! Stress is the worst thing
for this patient!

460
00:23:29,708 --> 00:23:31,710
I'm the one under stress!

461
00:23:31,777 --> 00:23:33,211
When there's no love,

462
00:23:33,712 --> 00:23:37,416
it's a worse breach of ethics
to remain as a married couple.

463
00:23:38,283 --> 00:23:40,218
How dare you say that!

464
00:23:40,285 --> 00:23:42,320
- Don't! Stop it!
- I won't stand for this!

465
00:23:43,288 --> 00:23:44,589
Stop!

466
00:23:45,924 --> 00:23:47,392
This is a hospital room.

467
00:23:47,459 --> 00:23:49,261
That's a patient. Get out.

468
00:23:49,327 --> 00:23:51,963
- Who do you think you are?
- Just get out!

469
00:23:53,899 --> 00:23:55,534
I am terribly sorry.

470
00:23:55,600 --> 00:23:57,536
Please, just step outside for now.

471
00:23:57,602 --> 00:23:59,204
- This way.
- Lie back.

472
00:24:00,439 --> 00:24:01,706
I'll get you some tea.

473
00:24:02,274 --> 00:24:03,408
Are you all right?

474
00:24:09,614 --> 00:24:10,982
Thank you.

475
00:24:13,251 --> 00:24:14,119
What?

476
00:24:23,195 --> 00:24:24,629
Dr. Daimon.

477
00:24:26,765 --> 00:24:31,336
I heard you're paying
a lot of attention to our PR chief.

478
00:24:31,403 --> 00:24:32,370
So?

479
00:24:32,904 --> 00:24:36,641
I'm sorry that you won't be able
to work on her.

480
00:24:38,677 --> 00:24:42,147
I wanted to see one of your beautiful…

481
00:24:42,781 --> 00:24:44,950
100% perfect surgeries.

482
00:24:52,123 --> 00:24:53,425
What's with that guy?

483
00:24:59,064 --> 00:25:00,432
SURGERY DEPARTMENT

484
00:25:06,805 --> 00:25:08,006
What do you want?

485
00:25:08,573 --> 00:25:10,742
I've come to tell you
something entertaining.

486
00:25:12,811 --> 00:25:17,382
We're all pretty stressed out,
so we would appreciate some laughter.

487
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:20,619
It's about PR Chief Mikuni.

488
00:25:21,119 --> 00:25:23,622
I found out the main reason
for her stress.

489
00:25:24,222 --> 00:25:25,323
What is it?

490
00:25:26,491 --> 00:25:28,960
Since it is a private matter,

491
00:25:29,027 --> 00:25:31,129
I can't talk about it publicly.

492
00:25:31,630 --> 00:25:35,367
Then we'll just keep it among us.

493
00:25:38,470 --> 00:25:39,704
It's lovesickness.

494
00:25:40,839 --> 00:25:41,740
Love?

495
00:25:43,808 --> 00:25:44,943
An affair.

496
00:25:45,010 --> 00:25:46,077
An affair?

497
00:25:46,645 --> 00:25:47,879
Sorry.

498
00:25:48,914 --> 00:25:52,717
This unshakeable iron lady sought comfort

499
00:25:52,784 --> 00:25:54,819
from a man who's married.

500
00:25:56,488 --> 00:26:00,625
You mean PR Chief Mikuni
and Vice Minister Kanbe

501
00:26:00,692 --> 00:26:02,594
had an unmentionable relationship?

502
00:26:02,661 --> 00:26:03,762
Exactly.

503
00:26:03,828 --> 00:26:08,533
Unless this huge source of stress
is removed, she cannot be healed.

504
00:26:11,102 --> 00:26:13,238
The Surgery Department could never do it.

505
00:26:14,172 --> 00:26:16,241
But Internal Medicine can?

506
00:26:18,310 --> 00:26:19,911
It is my specialty.

507
00:26:21,880 --> 00:26:22,714
Your specialty?

508
00:26:24,082 --> 00:26:26,851
When it comes
to sensitive romantic issues,

509
00:26:26,918 --> 00:26:28,687
experience is key.

510
00:26:35,594 --> 00:26:37,162
That's all for me now.

511
00:26:40,966 --> 00:26:43,501
What's so entertaining about that?

512
00:26:43,568 --> 00:26:45,637
What's with that guy?

513
00:26:51,810 --> 00:26:53,912
Hey! Look at this!

514
00:26:53,979 --> 00:26:57,749
It's already out!
An article about the PR chief's affair!

515
00:26:57,816 --> 00:26:58,883
Look!

516
00:26:58,950 --> 00:27:01,820
Oh, wow! That sure is fast.

517
00:27:01,886 --> 00:27:03,655
Someone must have leaked it.

518
00:27:03,722 --> 00:27:05,724
- Probably his wife.
- Really?

519
00:27:05,790 --> 00:27:08,760
With the illegal entertainment
and affair scandals all at once,

520
00:27:08,827 --> 00:27:11,463
PR Chief Mikuni will just have to resign.

521
00:27:11,529 --> 00:27:13,298
How frightening.

522
00:27:13,365 --> 00:27:14,265
But…

523
00:27:14,332 --> 00:27:18,069
if they break up because of this,
it would really stress her out.

524
00:27:18,136 --> 00:27:20,572
Takotsubo cardiomyopathy is also called

525
00:27:20,639 --> 00:27:23,742
"Broken Heart Syndrome."

526
00:27:25,276 --> 00:27:29,648
WE HAVE NO CHOICE BUT TO BREAK UP.
LET ME SAY THANK YOU ONE LAST TIME.

527
00:27:38,757 --> 00:27:40,558
<i>Triggered by a broken heart,</i>

528
00:27:40,625 --> 00:27:43,261
a sudden cardiac rupture occurs
and the heart stops.

529
00:27:44,129 --> 00:27:47,132
If that happened,
even you, Michiko, couldn't help her.

530
00:27:47,198 --> 00:27:49,801
- That's not true!
- No way.

531
00:27:51,569 --> 00:27:54,606
- Dr. Daimon! Help!
- What are you doing?

532
00:27:54,673 --> 00:27:56,708
- So noisy!
- Hey!

533
00:27:56,775 --> 00:27:59,544
- Take off your shoes!
- Demon! Listen to this!

534
00:27:59,611 --> 00:28:04,049
He said he had an idea for becoming
a tail that can't get cut off,

535
00:28:04,115 --> 00:28:05,350
but he just wanted to drink.

536
00:28:05,417 --> 00:28:06,584
I've had it with you!

537
00:28:06,651 --> 00:28:08,520
- Turn me into mincemeat! I don't care!
- No way!

538
00:28:08,586 --> 00:28:09,921
Not mincemeat!

539
00:28:09,988 --> 00:28:13,925
- I'm leaving!
- Wait right there, Hiromi Jonouchi!

540
00:28:13,992 --> 00:28:15,460
Don't use my first name!

541
00:28:15,527 --> 00:28:18,797
- I'm stressed, my stomach is killing me!
- Don't touch me!

542
00:28:18,863 --> 00:28:21,866
I'm so stressed, no matter how much
I drink, I don't get drunk!

543
00:28:21,933 --> 00:28:24,502
You are drunk. Stinking drunk!

544
00:28:24,569 --> 00:28:27,305
- What do we do, Akira?
- I don't know.

545
00:28:27,839 --> 00:28:28,740
They fell asleep.

546
00:28:29,541 --> 00:28:32,844
That's how stress affects petty people.

547
00:28:32,911 --> 00:28:34,813
- Poor guys.
- Yes.

548
00:28:37,749 --> 00:28:38,917
It's me.

549
00:28:39,684 --> 00:28:42,821
I want some advice on a romantic affair.

550
00:28:43,321 --> 00:28:44,622
Yes.

551
00:28:44,689 --> 00:28:47,759
How can you cause the least amount
of shock when breaking up?

552
00:28:49,728 --> 00:28:51,096
TODAY'S VISITING HOURS ARE OVER.

553
00:28:52,130 --> 00:28:55,100
A whole bottle? Fine.

554
00:28:55,166 --> 00:28:56,468
How about Dom Perignon?

555
00:28:57,836 --> 00:28:59,537
Okay, I'll be there soon.

556
00:29:20,525 --> 00:29:22,594
Thank you for everything you've done.

557
00:29:24,195 --> 00:29:25,530
Farewell.

558
00:29:26,531 --> 00:29:27,632
Choko…

559
00:29:36,341 --> 00:29:37,208
Just a minute.

560
00:29:37,275 --> 00:29:38,209
What?

561
00:29:56,394 --> 00:29:57,762
Did you take a photo?

562
00:29:58,596 --> 00:30:00,498
- What?
- What paper are you from?

563
00:30:00,565 --> 00:30:02,867
Oh, I'm sorry.

564
00:30:03,768 --> 00:30:05,270
This is me.

565
00:30:05,336 --> 00:30:06,204
TADASHI KUWAGATA

566
00:30:07,238 --> 00:30:08,173
You're a doctor?

567
00:30:08,239 --> 00:30:10,141
I'm Ms. Mikuni's doctor.

568
00:30:10,208 --> 00:30:11,042
I'm sorry.

569
00:30:16,748 --> 00:30:17,682
Sorry,

570
00:30:17,749 --> 00:30:20,652
but please do not come to see her again.

571
00:30:20,718 --> 00:30:22,320
It's not good for her health.

572
00:30:23,621 --> 00:30:24,889
What do you mean?

573
00:30:26,491 --> 00:30:29,527
It's your fault that she fell ill.

574
00:30:31,396 --> 00:30:32,230
My fault?

575
00:30:33,531 --> 00:30:36,835
Your relationship has caused her
a lot of stress.

576
00:30:38,736 --> 00:30:40,305
Please break up with her

577
00:30:40,872 --> 00:30:42,841
without injuring her heart too badly.

578
00:30:43,708 --> 00:30:45,043
Please.

579
00:31:11,402 --> 00:31:12,637
Step back!

580
00:31:13,638 --> 00:31:14,739
Stop right there!

581
00:31:16,541 --> 00:31:18,109
There he is!

582
00:31:19,177 --> 00:31:21,646
- Mr. Kanbe!
- Mr. Kanbe, about your affair!

583
00:31:21,713 --> 00:31:23,414
Was the article about your affair true?

584
00:31:23,481 --> 00:31:25,583
What does your wife have to say?

585
00:31:25,650 --> 00:31:27,952
Dr. Ebina, here.

586
00:31:28,019 --> 00:31:30,421
- Thanks.
- I got hangover meds.

587
00:31:30,488 --> 00:31:33,024
- We really overdid it, didn't we?
- We sure did.

588
00:31:33,658 --> 00:31:35,260
- How many pills?
- Two.

589
00:31:36,160 --> 00:31:37,495
Good morning!

590
00:31:38,296 --> 00:31:42,200
Oh, man.
The entertaining internist is back.

591
00:31:42,267 --> 00:31:43,434
What is it this time?

592
00:31:43,501 --> 00:31:46,271
Vice Minister Kanbe is streaming live
on the Internet.

593
00:31:47,005 --> 00:31:47,839
What?

594
00:31:50,041 --> 00:31:54,412
<i>Due to my rash behavior,</i>

595
00:31:54,913 --> 00:31:57,415
<i>I have caused trouble to those near me.</i>

596
00:31:57,482 --> 00:31:58,816
<i>I am deeply sorry.</i>

597
00:31:59,517 --> 00:32:04,589
<i>Regarding the alleged affair</i>
<i>and dinner with PR Chief Mikuni</i>

598
00:32:04,656 --> 00:32:06,090
<i>of Totei University Hospital,</i>

599
00:32:06,157 --> 00:32:08,326
allow me to say this.

600
00:32:12,196 --> 00:32:15,500
<i>The dinner with Ms. Mikuni</i>
<i>was not business entertainment,</i>

601
00:32:16,067 --> 00:32:17,268
<i>but a private dinner.</i>

602
00:32:18,303 --> 00:32:20,872
<i>I invited her out myself.</i>

603
00:32:22,540 --> 00:32:25,009
<i>I love her.</i>

604
00:32:26,544 --> 00:32:27,979
Hey!

605
00:32:28,046 --> 00:32:29,614
<i>You admit to having an affair?</i>

606
00:32:29,681 --> 00:32:33,017
I see. Looks like
it already had an effect.

607
00:32:34,452 --> 00:32:37,422
Yesterday, I spoke briefly
with Vice Minister Kanbe.

608
00:32:37,488 --> 00:32:39,691
As the attending physician, I warned him.

609
00:32:40,258 --> 00:32:43,161
He should settle things
the way a real man should.

610
00:32:43,728 --> 00:32:44,862
Seriously?

611
00:32:44,929 --> 00:32:49,300
This will remove a major portion
of her stress.

612
00:32:50,768 --> 00:32:53,137
<i>Though this is a personal affair,</i>

613
00:32:53,204 --> 00:32:58,343
<i>I submitted divorce papers</i>
<i>to the city office just now.</i>

614
00:33:06,751 --> 00:33:10,888
<i>I will marry Choko Mikuni.</i>

615
00:33:10,955 --> 00:33:12,991
<i>I will marry her.</i>

616
00:33:16,661 --> 00:33:17,895
This is bad!

617
00:33:19,897 --> 00:33:20,898
Magnificent.

618
00:33:20,965 --> 00:33:23,134
Absolutely magnificent!

619
00:33:23,634 --> 00:33:26,738
I administered the finest treatment
a doctor can give!

620
00:33:28,740 --> 00:33:30,141
Marry…

621
00:33:47,258 --> 00:33:48,659
What's bad?

622
00:33:48,726 --> 00:33:50,895
Happy Heart Syndrome.

623
00:33:50,962 --> 00:33:53,264
Not only unpleasant events or stress

624
00:33:53,331 --> 00:33:54,899
trigger Takotsubo cardiomyopathy.

625
00:33:54,966 --> 00:33:58,002
- It can be triggered by happiness as well.
- What?

626
00:34:02,740 --> 00:34:03,574
VF!

627
00:34:03,641 --> 00:34:05,910
VENTRICULAR FIBRILLATION

628
00:34:08,613 --> 00:34:10,348
- I'll intubate her.
- Right.

629
00:34:10,415 --> 00:34:11,516
I'll get a DC.

630
00:34:14,786 --> 00:34:16,120
Dr. Daimon!

631
00:34:16,187 --> 00:34:17,822
Prep for emergency surgery!

632
00:34:17,889 --> 00:34:18,790
Right!

633
00:34:42,280 --> 00:34:45,083
Cardiac tamponade.
I'll open the pericardium.

634
00:34:45,149 --> 00:34:46,918
- Scalpel.
- Here.

635
00:35:02,066 --> 00:35:03,401
- Metz.
- Here.

636
00:35:20,718 --> 00:35:21,619
Why?

637
00:35:21,686 --> 00:35:22,820
Idiot.

638
00:35:23,354 --> 00:35:25,156
He went sticking his nose in her business.

639
00:35:25,656 --> 00:35:27,859
Damn that vice director
of Internal Medicine.

640
00:35:28,860 --> 00:35:30,094
Dr. Daimon,

641
00:35:30,161 --> 00:35:32,864
her heart won't survive that operation.

642
00:35:33,531 --> 00:35:35,066
I'll make it survive.

643
00:35:37,635 --> 00:35:38,903
Removing hematoma.

644
00:35:51,983 --> 00:35:53,818
The left ventricular free wall ruptured!

645
00:35:53,885 --> 00:35:55,653
More hemorrhaging than expected!

646
00:35:56,420 --> 00:35:58,556
BP dropped to 40s.

647
00:36:05,897 --> 00:36:07,431
What will you do, Dr. Daimon?

648
00:36:16,374 --> 00:36:17,341
- Gauze.
- Here.

649
00:36:22,847 --> 00:36:24,148
Dr. Daimon,

650
00:36:24,215 --> 00:36:27,418
apply a tissue adhesion sheet
and end the surgery.

651
00:36:28,186 --> 00:36:29,887
You want to kill the patient?

652
00:36:29,954 --> 00:36:31,923
Better than killing by surgery!

653
00:36:31,989 --> 00:36:33,925
This surgery is not 100% certain!

654
00:36:33,991 --> 00:36:36,694
Didn't you want to watch me operate?

655
00:36:38,529 --> 00:36:40,565
Then shut up and watch!

656
00:36:41,132 --> 00:36:42,166
I,

657
00:36:43,167 --> 00:36:45,469
100%, will not fail.

658
00:37:04,989 --> 00:37:07,592
I found the rupture. I'll suture it.

659
00:37:07,658 --> 00:37:09,627
- Spread the sternal retracter.
- Okay.

660
00:37:09,694 --> 00:37:11,762
- Lower my loupes.
- Yes, ma'am.

661
00:37:12,496 --> 00:37:14,498
- 3-0 monofilament.
- Here.

662
00:37:31,315 --> 00:37:32,483
Repairs complete.

663
00:37:33,317 --> 00:37:34,518
Hemorrhaging stopped.

664
00:37:34,585 --> 00:37:36,988
Now, for the coronary artery bypass.

665
00:37:37,054 --> 00:37:39,090
Ablating internal artery.
Ultrasonic scalpel.

666
00:37:39,156 --> 00:37:40,124
Here.

667
00:37:59,744 --> 00:38:00,578
Vitals?

668
00:38:00,645 --> 00:38:04,982
BP 128 over 78, pulse 78, normal sinus.

669
00:38:07,218 --> 00:38:08,586
Thank goodness.

670
00:38:09,887 --> 00:38:10,955
- Done.
- Nice work.

671
00:38:19,363 --> 00:38:20,631
Nice work.

672
00:38:20,698 --> 00:38:21,999
You too.

673
00:38:41,952 --> 00:38:45,456
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a maverick woman doctor.</i>

674
00:38:48,225 --> 00:38:49,493
Excuse me.

675
00:38:50,061 --> 00:38:54,932
I would like to thank you for employing
Dr. Daimon and Dr. Jonouchi.

676
00:38:56,367 --> 00:38:59,370
I appreciate you coming all this way,

677
00:38:59,437 --> 00:39:03,040
but those two operated without permission.

678
00:39:03,107 --> 00:39:04,809
However,

679
00:39:05,576 --> 00:39:07,211
I understand that their actions

680
00:39:07,278 --> 00:39:09,180
were extremely beneficial to you,

681
00:39:09,246 --> 00:39:10,314
Branch Director Hiruma.

682
00:39:11,816 --> 00:39:13,317
Beneficial to me?

683
00:39:13,884 --> 00:39:15,152
What do you mean?

684
00:39:15,219 --> 00:39:19,223
The right hand of Director
of Internal Medicine Hachisuka,

685
00:39:19,290 --> 00:39:20,591
PR Chief Mikuni,

686
00:39:20,658 --> 00:39:21,592
was saved

687
00:39:21,659 --> 00:39:23,994
by the hospital's Surgery Department.

688
00:39:24,061 --> 00:39:27,732
Now, they owe you a great big favor.

689
00:39:27,798 --> 00:39:31,802
I don't think there could be
any bigger benefit than that.

690
00:39:33,404 --> 00:39:34,605
That's for sure.

691
00:39:35,373 --> 00:39:39,510
But how you use that benefit

692
00:39:39,577 --> 00:39:41,679
depends on your…

693
00:39:43,881 --> 00:39:44,849
ability.

694
00:39:46,450 --> 00:39:48,686
- This?
- Right.

695
00:39:48,753 --> 00:39:50,788
- Allow me to be frank.
- Yes?

696
00:39:50,855 --> 00:39:54,825
Having to call the man
who was once the head

697
00:39:54,892 --> 00:40:00,297
of Totei University Hospital
"Branch Director" pains me terribly.

698
00:40:00,364 --> 00:40:02,199
I look forward to the day

699
00:40:02,266 --> 00:40:06,103
that the word "branch"
is removed from your title.

700
00:40:06,670 --> 00:40:08,339
- You do?
- Yes.

701
00:40:08,406 --> 00:40:09,507
This is a melon.

702
00:40:11,142 --> 00:40:12,777
This is the bill.

703
00:40:15,613 --> 00:40:16,614
Shall I look?

704
00:40:16,680 --> 00:40:17,715
Go right ahead.

705
00:40:20,017 --> 00:40:21,852
SURGICAL FEES FOR DR. DAIMON

706
00:40:22,520 --> 00:40:25,055
As expensive as ever.

707
00:40:25,122 --> 00:40:27,425
I am so very grateful,

708
00:40:27,491 --> 00:40:29,093
Director Hiruma.

709
00:40:29,794 --> 00:40:31,529
Wait. What did you say?

710
00:40:31,595 --> 00:40:33,364
I said "Director Hiruma."

711
00:40:36,033 --> 00:40:37,701
Say it again.

712
00:40:37,768 --> 00:40:39,236
Director Hiruma.

713
00:40:39,303 --> 00:40:40,771
- Director Hiruma!
- Yes?

714
00:40:40,838 --> 00:40:42,473
- Director Hiruma.
- Yes?

715
00:40:42,540 --> 00:40:43,941
- Shall I come in again?
- Yes, do.

716
00:40:44,008 --> 00:40:47,311
- Come in!
- Excuse me, Director Hiruma!

717
00:40:47,378 --> 00:40:49,914
- I like it!
- I'll be going now.

718
00:40:49,980 --> 00:40:52,750
- I like it!
- Thank you, Director Hiruma!

719
00:40:52,817 --> 00:40:53,651
Oh, yes!

720
00:40:53,717 --> 00:40:55,386
- Thank you!
- Goodbye!

721
00:40:55,953 --> 00:40:59,290
Thank you for saving my life.

722
00:40:59,356 --> 00:41:02,660
It was Dr. Daimon who saved you.

723
00:41:04,161 --> 00:41:07,465
I know how to take responsibility
for what I've done.

724
00:41:08,666 --> 00:41:11,101
RESIGNATION

725
00:41:13,604 --> 00:41:16,674
I am sorry
I was unable to be of assistance.

726
00:41:18,742 --> 00:41:19,910
Please accept it.

727
00:41:22,346 --> 00:41:24,615
From the very start,

728
00:41:25,149 --> 00:41:27,885
you had it all planned out, didn't you?

729
00:41:29,186 --> 00:41:30,488
What are you talking about?

730
00:41:32,289 --> 00:41:33,524
You…

731
00:41:34,058 --> 00:41:37,628
intentionally leaked to the press
the day and time

732
00:41:37,695 --> 00:41:40,564
of the dinner that I had arranged

733
00:41:40,631 --> 00:41:42,867
and had photos taken. Isn't that right?

734
00:41:43,901 --> 00:41:46,971
<i>You also leaked the story</i>
<i>about your affair.</i>

735
00:41:48,973 --> 00:41:53,410
You did a magnificent job
of obtaining strong connections

736
00:41:53,477 --> 00:41:55,913
with the Ministry of Health.

737
00:41:57,815 --> 00:41:59,416
What do you mean by that?

738
00:42:02,152 --> 00:42:03,254
From now on,

739
00:42:05,289 --> 00:42:07,391
make good use

740
00:42:08,125 --> 00:42:11,262
of your marriage to Vice Minister Kanbe.

741
00:42:11,795 --> 00:42:15,666
For Totei University, and me.

742
00:42:20,671 --> 00:42:22,506
I appreciate your assistance.

743
00:42:26,677 --> 00:42:29,146
If you're going that far…

744
00:42:32,016 --> 00:42:33,551
RESIGNATION

745
00:42:35,352 --> 00:42:37,721
I will let my husband know.

746
00:42:51,368 --> 00:42:52,703
Michiko? What's wrong?

747
00:42:52,770 --> 00:42:55,339
- Are you hungry?
- I'm starving!

748
00:42:55,406 --> 00:42:58,242
- Oh, all right.
- I know! Meat!

749
00:42:58,309 --> 00:43:00,210
<i>She hates groups,</i>

750
00:43:00,978 --> 00:43:03,347
<i>she hates authorities,</i>

751
00:43:03,414 --> 00:43:05,316
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

752
00:43:05,382 --> 00:43:08,385
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill</i>

753
00:43:08,452 --> 00:43:10,421
<i>to work her way up.</i>

754
00:43:10,487 --> 00:43:12,189
- I can?
- Yes.

755
00:43:12,256 --> 00:43:13,924
- By myself?
- Yes.

756
00:43:17,394 --> 00:43:18,696
Dr. Daimon.

757
00:43:20,030 --> 00:43:22,766
Thanks to you, everything went perfectly.

758
00:43:22,833 --> 00:43:23,801
Thank you.

759
00:43:24,435 --> 00:43:26,670
- You're welcome.
- Remember what you said?

760
00:43:27,404 --> 00:43:29,707
"There's no point in dying from your job."

761
00:43:30,674 --> 00:43:32,009
But I don't mind.

762
00:43:32,076 --> 00:43:35,012
I am willing to die for my work.

763
00:43:36,280 --> 00:43:38,916
You're amazing, PR Chief Mikuni.

764
00:43:38,983 --> 00:43:41,285
You are the perfect empress.

765
00:43:41,352 --> 00:43:42,353
What do you mean?

766
00:43:42,419 --> 00:43:44,955
You suffered a cardiac rupture,

767
00:43:45,022 --> 00:43:46,890
not because of marriage,

768
00:43:46,957 --> 00:43:50,961
but because you gained control
of the head of the Ministry of Health.

769
00:43:53,631 --> 00:43:56,100
You'll climb even higher.

770
00:43:56,166 --> 00:43:58,335
That made you so happy,

771
00:43:58,402 --> 00:44:01,705
it triggered
a Happy Heart Syndrome, right?

772
00:44:03,974 --> 00:44:06,610
Why don't you team up with me

773
00:44:07,144 --> 00:44:08,679
and aim even higher?

774
00:44:08,746 --> 00:44:10,514
I think you and I could do it.

775
00:44:11,348 --> 00:44:13,283
I'm not interested in status.

776
00:44:14,284 --> 00:44:15,653
Is that so?

777
00:44:15,719 --> 00:44:16,754
How unfortunate.

778
00:44:16,820 --> 00:44:18,088
Goodbye.

779
00:44:19,323 --> 00:44:21,692
She's a determined one.

780
00:44:21,759 --> 00:44:23,961
She never lets her prey get away.

781
00:44:24,028 --> 00:44:26,397
She's like a woman octopus jar trap.

782
00:44:27,264 --> 00:44:29,833
- Octopus!
- What?

783
00:44:30,567 --> 00:44:32,269
- What?
- I want <i>takoyaki!</i>

784
00:44:32,336 --> 00:44:34,204
- Really? <i>Takoyaki</i> is okay?
- Yes!

785
00:44:34,271 --> 00:44:36,206
I want <i>takoyaki.</i> Where should we get it?

786
00:44:36,273 --> 00:44:38,142
How about the usual place?

787
00:44:38,208 --> 00:44:43,280
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

788
00:44:44,081 --> 00:44:46,050
<i>I want to return to rehearsals quickly.</i>

789
00:44:46,116 --> 00:44:47,217
<i>This situation is critical!</i>

790
00:44:47,284 --> 00:44:48,218
I won't operate.

791
00:44:48,285 --> 00:44:51,321
<i>If she is not cured via surgery,</i>
<i>submit your resignation!</i>

792
00:44:51,388 --> 00:44:52,423
What will I do now?

793
00:44:52,489 --> 00:44:54,591
<i>I want to be in this musical</i>
<i>even if it kills me.</i>

794
00:44:54,658 --> 00:44:55,693
I want to sing!

795
00:44:55,759 --> 00:44:58,262
- Dr. Daimon, I beg you! Operate!
- I won't let anyone's neck get cut.

796
00:44:58,328 --> 00:44:59,329
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
